  "notes": "Wichita program offerings confirmed by Galen's official Wichita campus page (https://galencollege.edu/wichita-ks): LPN/LVN to ADN Bridge and 2-Year ADN; campus at 551 N. Hillside Street, Suite 410, Wichita, KS 67214-4923. The Kansas WIOA training-institution listing for this campus describes the Bridge as 99 quarter credits / 72 weeks, ACEN-accredited, Associate of Science. Quarter-by-quarter Program of Study is Galen's standard institution-wide ADN curriculum, taken from Appendix A of Galen's official 'Application for Intent to Open a Physical Building and Establish a Nursing Education Program: Associate Degree in Nursing Program' submitted to the Utah Board of Nursing (October 24, 2022; updated February 22, 2023) — the filing states the ADN 'is currently offered at other Galen campuses, has an existing faculty-developed curriculum' and that branch campuses are supervised by the Main Campus in Louisville, KY under consistent policies. Galen runs on a QUARTER calendar; seeded as published in quarters. Sequenced sum = 79 quarter credits; the filing additionally awards 20 quarter credits 'Credit for PN/VN Licensure' (NOT sequenced), for a total degree requirement of 99 quarter credits (matching the Kansas listing). Admission requires proof of active, unencumbered PN/VN licensure and diploma. Downstream semester-gated checks (associate 4-7 / bachelor 8-12 semester gates) are semester-calibrated and do not apply to quarter terms without conversion. No course-level prerequisites are listed in the plan of study tables.",
